This dossier supports first-time, never-licensed applicants preparing for the regular passenger-car written knowledge and road sign tests in Michigan. The issuing authority is the Michigan Department of State, led by the Secretary of State, and the source is the handbook What Every Driver Must Know. This section covers safe driving across age groups, aggressive driving and road rage, intersection safety, freeway entry, lane use, HOV lanes, the merge law, exiting and missed exits, freeway fatigue, cruise control, an oncoming vehicle in your lane, winter preparation, rain, hydroplaning, flooded roads, fog, ice and snow, skids, and braking with and without anti-lock brakes. The handbook pages do not state an official question count, passing score, test format or time limit for the Secretary of State knowledge test, so this dossier asserts no value for any of them and records each as an explicit unknown. Practice scoring follows only the accepted LearningLoop product policy, never an official threshold.
